/-!
# Candidate-A zero modes generated by infinitesimal symmetries

The named-mode frontier formerly stored the equation `H v = 0` for every
physical mode.  This file derives that equation from a local Noether statement:
the gradient of the genuine common augmented Candidate-A action is invariant
along the affine orbit generated by the mode.

Once annihilation is derived, the existing automatic orthogonal splitting and
global Gårding estimate exclude hidden zero modes, construct the exact kernel,
and produce the actual-kernel gap used by H12.  Thus the terminal input no
longer contains a hand-written kernel-membership proof for each symmetry mode.
-/

